    "body": "Fix the version string before tagging v0.4.0. Without this, a git checkout v0.4.0 would build a binary that reports \"HoneyBee Browser v0.3.0\" on startup -- the same drift that v0.2.0 and v0.3.0 shipped with, requiring v0.2.1 and v0.3.1 patch releases.\n\nThe v0.4.0 tag has not been created yet. This PR fixes the version first, then the tag lands on the corrected commit.\n\n## What changed\n\n- CMakeLists.txt: VERSION 0.3.0 -> VERSION 0.4.0\n- src/base/version.cpp: string + minor (3->4); patch unchanged (0)\n- tests/test_version.cpp: 2 assertions updated\n- src/base/version.hpp: doc comment example\n\n## Verification\n\n- 213 cases, 839 assertions, all pass\n- Banner after this PR: HoneyBee Browser v0.4.0\n\n## Why this is first\n\nSame three-file pattern as v0.2.1 and v0.3.1, but applied BEFORE the tag rather than as a patch release after. Breaking the drift pattern rather than repeating it.\n\n## After merge\n\nTag v0.4.0 at the merge commit, push to both remotes, publish GitHub release with notes covering ADR-016 (inline formatting, display, dir attribute). No version-drift caveat in the release notes because there will be no drift.\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-21T11:49:35Z",
